Q14) Melt
Pivot builds a matrix.
Melt destroys the matrix.
converts long format to wide

Instead of:
“What becomes rows or columns?”
Melt asks:
“Which columns should stay fixed, and which ones should collapse?

var_name = “what this column used to be called”
value_name = “what was in that column”

A14)
melted = pd.melt(
    report,
    id_vars="product",       # keep the product column fixed
    var_name="quarter",      # column names to a new column
    value_name="sales"       # values go into this new column
)

